  "summary": "DarkMe is a Visual Basic 6 spy-RAT attributed to Water Hydra (EvilNum/Operation DarkCasino) that in this campaign dropped zero-days in favour of an email-delivered image.pif that fetches a remote exemsi-wrapped MSI. The MSI expands a CAB into %AppData%\\ComponentsFolder, runs prnfig.wsf to register a COM object and a custom Locked:// protocol handler, then loads three VB6 loader DLLs that gate on 329 user applications and hollow Microsoft-signed clspack.exe. The injected RAT profiles the host, steals crypto wallets and screenshots, and beacons over a custom TCP channel on port 7712 to an RC4-encrypted C2 domain.",
